---
description: Security rules. Use when a change touches authentication, authorization, uploads, headers, CSP, secrets, accounts, rate limits or dependencies.
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow "Security rules" and "Do not" in @AGENTS.md, and @SECURITY.md for
the policy and production checklist. In short:

- Never commit secrets, real credentials or personal data; never seed
  privileged accounts.
- Every authenticated `/api` route stays in the `auth:api` + `verified`
  group in `routes/api.php`.
- Uploads go through `App\Actions\Products\StoreProductImage`.
- Do not weaken `App\Http\Middleware\SecurityHeaders`, the rate limiters in
  `AppServiceProvider`, or the tests that check them.
- Report vulnerabilities privately (see SECURITY.md), never in a public
  issue.
